extends ../../layouts/home

append config
  -pageName = 'Article'

block content
  .container.py-5
    //- Breadcrumb
    nav.mb-5(aria-label="breadcrumb")
      ol.breadcrumb.small
        li.breadcrumb-item: a.text-decoration-none.text-body-secondary(href=`${baseUrl}blog/blog.html`) Blog
        li.breadcrumb-item.active(aria-current='page') Modern UI Design

    .row.gx-lg-5
      //- Main Content Column
      .col-lg-8 

        // Post Article
        article.mb-5
            // Post header
            header.mb-5
              .mb-4.d-flex.flex-wrap.gap-2
                a.badge.bg-primary.bg-opacity-10.text-primary.text-decoration-none.px-3.py-2(href='#!') Design
                a.badge.bg-secondary.bg-opacity-10.text-secondary.text-decoration-none.px-3.py-2(href='#!') UI/UX

              h1.fw-bold.display-4.mb-4 Designing without Borders and Shadows
              
              .d-flex.align-items-center.gap-3.pb-4.border-bottom.border-body-secondary
                .avatar.rounded-circle.bg-primary.bg-opacity-10.text-primary.d-flex.align-items-center.justify-content-center.fw-bold(style="width: 48px; height: 48px;") PL
                div
                    .fw-bold.text-body PiruLUG
                    .small.text-body-secondary Published on Jan 1, 2024 • 5 min read

            //- Main Image
            figure.mb-5.rounded.overflow-hidden
              img.img-fluid.w-100(src='https://dummyimage.com/1200x600/181818/f8f9fa&text=Modern+UI+Design' alt='Modern UI' style="max-height: 500px; object-fit: cover;")

            // Post content
            section.lh-lg.fs-5.text-body-secondary
              p.mb-4.lead.text-body The evolution of web design has led us to cleaner and more streamlined interfaces. The current trend moves away from hard borders and heavy shadows, seeking a visual hierarchy based on negative spacing and subtle background tone shifts.
              
              p.mb-4 By removing borders, we allow the content to breathe. Elements are logically grouped through the intelligent use of padding, creating a much more fluid and professional reading experience.
              
              blockquote.blockquote.my-5.p-4.p-md-5.bg-body.rounded.border-start.border-primary.border-5
                p.mb-3.fw-medium.text-body.fst-italic "Design is not just what it looks like and feels like. Design is how it works. And functional minimalism is the key to user retention."
                footer.blockquote-footer.small Adapted from Steve Jobs
              
              h2.fw-bold.text-body.mt-5.mb-4 Why Borderless Works
              
              p.mb-4 
                strong 1. Less visual fatigue: 
                | Without hard lines to process, the eye focuses on what really matters: the content.
              p.mb-4 
                strong 2. Modernity: 
                | Reflects a sophisticated and contemporary design language.
              p.mb-4 
                strong 3. Adaptability: 
                | Works exceptionally well in both light and dark themes.

        //- Share & CTA
        section.py-5.border-top.border-bottom.border-body-secondary.mb-5
          .row.align-items-center.gy-4
            .col-md-6
               h5.fw-bold.mb-0 Did you like this post?
               p.text-body-secondary.small.mb-0 Share it with your network.
            .col-md-6.text-md-end
               .d-flex.gap-2.justify-content-md-end
                  a.btn.btn-sm.bg-body.px-3(href="#"): i.bi.bi-facebook
                  a.btn.btn-sm.bg-body.px-3(href="#"): i.bi.bi-twitter-x
                  a.btn.btn-sm.bg-body.px-3(href="#"): i.bi.bi-linkedin
        
        //- Comments section
        section.py-5
          h4.fw-bold.mb-5 Comments (3)
          
          .d-grid.gap-4
            // Comment 1
            .d-flex.gap-3.p-4.bg-body.rounded
              .avatar.rounded-circle.bg-secondary.bg-opacity-10.text-secondary.flex-shrink-0.d-flex.align-items-center.justify-content-center.fw-bold(style="width: 48px; height: 48px;") AN
              div
                  .d-flex.justify-content-between.align-items-center.mb-1
                      .fw-bold Anonymous User
                      .text-muted.x-small 2 hours ago
                  p.text-body-secondary.small.mb-0 Incredible article. I've been applying the borderless style in my latest projects and the difference in visual cleanliness is abysmal.
            
            // Comment 2
            .d-flex.gap-3.p-4.bg-body.rounded
              .avatar.rounded-circle.bg-primary.bg-opacity-10.text-primary.flex-shrink-0.d-flex.align-items-center.justify-content-center.fw-bold(style="width: 48px; height: 48px;") MG
              div
                  .d-flex.justify-content-between.align-items-center.mb-1
                      .fw-bold Maria Gomez
                      .text-muted.x-small 5 hours ago
                  p.text-body-secondary.small.mb-0 I love the use of hierarchies by background color. Very inspiring.
          
          //- Action CTA
          .mt-5.p-5.bg-body.rounded.text-center
            h5.fw-bold Leave your opinion
            p.text-body-secondary.mb-4 Join the conversation and share your thoughts.
            button.btn.btn-primary.px-5.fw-bold Login to comment

      //- Sidebar Column
      .col-lg-4
        include ../../includes/blog-aside

